course: dictionary
lesson: 9232
title: Songbird: a bird or a singer
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A songbird is a small bird that sings tuneful songs. Robins, blackbirds, thrushes, nightingales and wrens are all songbirds. When you meet the word, look at the words around it for clues.
explain: «In spring male songbirds such as blackbirds sing at dawn to claim territory and be noticed.» The clues are spring, sing and dawn, so a songbird must be a bird that sings. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: The word can also describe a person. Informally, a person, usually a woman, with a lovely singing voice can be called a songbird. If the sentence is about a singer and not a bird, this second meaning is the right one.
explain: Scientists use the word for a big group of birds. «Falcons look like hawks, but DNA shows they are closer cousins of parrots and songbirds.» Here songbirds means a whole group of perching birds, not just one kind of bird.
fact: A songbird is a small bird that sings tuneful songs.
fact: Robins, blackbirds, thrushes, nightingales and wrens are songbirds.
fact: Songbirds sing to mark their territory and to find a mate, often at dawn in spring.
fact: Informally, a person with a lovely singing voice can be called a songbird.
fact: Young songbirds learn their songs by listening and practising.
exercise: «Male songbirds sing at dawn in spring to claim territory.» What is a songbird? | A large bird that cannot fly | *A small bird that sings tuneful songs | A fish that swims in rivers | A bird that only lives in the sea
exercise: Which of these is a songbird? | An eagle | A penguin | *A robin | A hawk
exercise: Lily says, «Maya is a real songbird, she sang beautifully at assembly.» What does songbird mean here? | A bird that has lost its song | A small brown bird in a tree | *A person with a lovely singing voice | A bird that can talk
test: «Young birds learn their songs by listening and practising, much like a baby learning to talk.» What do young songbirds learn by doing? | *Listening and practising | Building nests alone | Flying south for the winter | Eating worms all day
test: Falcons are closer cousins of which birds, according to DNA? | Penguins and ducks | Hawks and eagles | *Parrots and songbirds | Owls and pigeons
exam: Which sentence uses songbird for a person? | *«The songbird at the school concert sang so sweetly that the hall went quiet.» | «The songbird flew into the nest.» | «Songbirds gathered on the garden fence.» | «The songbirds sang at dawn in the wood.»
